{
  "v": 1,
  "about": "Tin Hat notification actions (docs/NOTIF-ACTIONS.md): Reply and Mark as read on a message notification. Byte-identical copies: web src/features/push/testvectors/notifactions.json (the owner), desktop crates/app/src/testvectors/notifactions.json. whitespace = the code points trimmed from both ends of a reply after CRLF and lone CR became LF. replyContent: the typed text -> the m.room.message content to send (null = nothing is sent). readMarkers: the notified event in a room of my own server -> the POST /rooms/{room}/read_markers body (null = no Mark as read; event id rule: '$' + 1..254 more UTF-8 bytes, no control, white-space or listed white-space characters). offer: what a message notification carries (keys in order; 'default' = the click). outcome: an invoked key (publicReceipt = the receiptRule answer for the room) -> what the app does (open = open the room; compose = open it with the composer focused; send = send content then thenRead when present; read = send markers; failed = post the failure note with that body; none = nothing). failedNote: the failure note's body for a typed text (first failedTextMax code points of the trimmed text). receiptRule: which read receipt a room gets (Mark as read, and every receipt both apps send): a public m.read only when the room is mine = isManaged(create, own) (the m.room.create sender and every v12 additional_creators entry on my own server); anything else, a missing create event (null) included, gets m.read.private next to m.fully_read. Fail-private on purpose: rooms on connected Tin Hat servers get m.read.private too until the connected-servers list exists. The phone apps (iOS, Android) adopt these cases too.",
